WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.560
- She's obviously a tense moment.

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:04.050
There's a lot of talk about
the counter offensive.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.663
Is there anything you
can tell us about that?

00:00:06.663 --> 00:00:10.580
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:25.800
It's the eve of the counter offensive

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.600
that the world has been waiting for.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:29.820
At one of the most consequential
moments since the war

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.590
in Ukraine began.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:34.230
We traveled to the southern
port city of Odessa

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.390
to talk to the man at
the center of it all,

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:38.850
President Volodymyr Zelensky.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.130
He was about to meet European leaders

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:44.430
to press for membership of
the European Union and NATO.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:45.780
The big question,

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.990
how to cement Ukraine's
long-term security.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.090
The big problem, I guess for you

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:53.070
and for the world is Putin

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.110
and the people around him still think

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.670
that they should be here.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.770
So what does that mean for Ukraine

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.900
and what does it mean for the, you know,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.439
the Western Alliance.

00:01:02.439 --> 00:01:06.356
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:38.100
(speaking in foreign language continues)

00:02:00.001 --> 00:02:04.751
(speaking in foreign language continues)

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:26.280
So obviously, you talking all the time

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:28.290
to your allies and you know,

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.990
there is going to be an
election in the US next year.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.310
Does that worry you

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.170
because there could be a change

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:36.090
should Donald Trump win again?

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.950
Does that create a pressure on Ukraine

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.812
to sort of get the war finished?

00:02:39.812 --> 00:02:43.729
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:06.733
(speaking in foreign language continues)

00:03:29.665 --> 00:03:34.415
(speaking in foreign language continues)

00:03:59.401 --> 00:04:04.339
(speaking in foreign language continues)

00:04:04.339 --> 00:04:06.870
President Zelensky told me he
doesn't have enough firepower

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.730
to defend his entire country.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:10.620
While I was in Keith,
the night was punctuated

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.083
by loud explosions of missiles and drones.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.980
Zelensky believes this is
Putin showing him that he needs

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.040
to make a choice protect
his cities or his troops

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.360
on the front line.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.800
He says he can't do both

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.500
with the amount of weapons he has.

00:04:25.713 --> 00:04:29.630
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:54.498 --> 00:04:59.248
(speaking in foreign language continues)

00:05:26.813 --> 00:05:31.563
(speaking in foreign language continues)

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.670
NATO will hold its next
summit in Vilnius, Lithuania

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:48.930
in July.

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:51.630
Pressure is grown to give
Ukraine security guarantees

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:53.520
and a path to membership.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.560
Zelensky says he needs an explicit sign

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:57.060
that this will happen.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:00.661
Are you optimistic that NATO
will admit you as a member?

00:06:00.661 --> 00:06:04.578
(speaking in foreign language)

00:06:25.268 --> 00:06:30.018
(speaking in foreign language continues)

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:58.953
Do you think you'll get that statement?

00:06:59.854 --> 00:07:03.771
(speaking in foreign language)

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:06.810
What do you want from China?

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:08.430
You know, they are friendly with Russia.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.740
What do you want or expect from China?

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:15.657
(speaking in foreign language)

00:07:32.374 --> 00:07:37.124
(speaking in foreign language continues)

00:07:38.939 --> 00:07:40.740
Before I sat down for this interview,

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:44.070
I followed Zelensky to a hospital
to visit wounded soldiers.

00:07:44.070 --> 00:07:46.620
He spoke to a soldier
who had lost both hands

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:48.990
and comforted the young man's partner.

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:53.070
I saw firsthand how Zelensky
is facing the pain, suffering

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:56.250
and sadness that has come with this war.

00:07:56.250 --> 00:07:59.220
So this was the first time
I'd seen the war up close

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:03.120
and it hit me like a,
I was very emotional.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.280
You have to go in and
speak to the soldiers,

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.530
speak to the mother that
was standing outside.

00:08:07.530 --> 00:08:12.525
I mean, how do you keep your morale up?

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:16.442
(speaking in foreign language)

00:08:35.582 --> 00:08:38.790
You obviously never stop
working and even someone

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:42.450
who's at war has to find time to relax.

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:43.953
How do you switch off?

00:08:44.970 --> 00:08:46.970
How do you ever relax?

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:48.750
(speaking in foreign language)

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:49.874
What do you read?

00:08:49.874 --> 00:08:53.791
(speaking in foreign language)

00:09:03.672 --> 00:09:06.218
I don't suppose you
get much time for them.

00:09:06.218 --> 00:09:08.910
(speaking in foreign language)

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.610
(both laughing)

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:12.870
- Very smart.
- Yes!

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:14.160
- I think so.

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:16.651
No-
- Check the kids' homework.

00:09:16.651 --> 00:09:18.000
Aren't you?
(both laughing)

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.370
- No English.

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:21.210
- Oh, check their English.
- English with my son.

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:22.043
- Good, good.

00:09:22.043 --> 00:09:24.330
And Harry's, his English, is it coming on?

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:26.430
- I think his English is better.

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:27.810
- Oh.
(both laughing)

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.100
You can practice with him!

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.030
Yeah.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:30.863
That's wonderful.

00:09:30.863 --> 00:09:31.860
- No, my daughter,

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:34.440
she knows English very well.
- Yes.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.710
- She's better teacher for my son than me.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.510
But sometimes when I see my son,

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.190
I want just to have some time

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:42.090
with him.
- Yes.

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:45.150
- And when even it
doesn't matter what to do.

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:46.371
- Yeah.
- I mean that-

00:09:46.371 --> 00:09:47.280
- Just time.
- Just time.

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:48.330
- Yeah, exactly.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:50.970
And time is the one thing
you don't have very much of,

00:09:50.970 --> 00:09:51.971
right.

00:09:51.971 --> 00:09:55.888
(speaking in foreign language)

